# Pairs with AtomicOnOwner. #4632's guard with the coordinator's participant
# row registered best-effort, as the bulk pre-registration was before the fix
# made it a precondition of the first dispatch: the row may be missing while
# the saga is live, so a live saga's hot-path forward during the split window
# is refused silently at the destination, and once the split moves the key
# the owner serves the pre-saga value next to the committed other key. The
# edit lies in PRow, the operator the guard reads, so the mutation declares no
# PERTURBS.
MODULE: AtomicOnOwnerParticipantRowBestEffort
TARGET: AtomicOnOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: with a best-effort participant row the guard refuses a live saga's forward, tearing the batch

--- FIND
PRow == sg # "idle" /\ ~forgotten
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the row exists only once the decision is recorded.
PRow == dec # "none" /\ ~forgotten
--- END